---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, AUTHOR_ROLE, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_URL, SITE_NAMES, LEGAL, LANG_TAGS } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { personSchema, organizationSchema, breadcrumbSchema, profilePageSchema, contactPageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const upd = displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, LANG_TAGS[lang]);
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy: Your Passport Dates Never Leave Your Browser" description="Privacy policy of US Passport Cost: ages, issue dates, travel dates and choices are calculated in your browser and never sent; no cookies, no forms, only host logs." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>2. What you type</h2>
    <p>Your situation, age, passport dates, destination and travel dates are processed only by your browser. <strong>Nothing is sent to us or to anyone else and nothing is stored.</strong> After you change a field, your choices are written into the address bar of your own browser so that you can copy the link; that address is not transmitted unless you share it.</p>
    <h2>3. What the host sees</h2>
    <p>When a page loads, the host processes technical data needed to deliver it: IP address, time, page requested, browser and referring page. Legal basis: legitimate interest in running the site (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR, as the publisher is in France).</p>
    <h2>4. Measurement</h2>
    <p>No cookies are set. If anonymous error measurement (Microsoft Clarity, cookieless mode) is switched on, it records loading errors and load times with every form field masked. Provider: Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, Dublin, Ireland.</p>
    <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You may ask for access, correction, deletion or objection by writing to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we answer within a month. You may also complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>). Visitors in California keep the rights given by the CCPA; we sell and share no personal information. See also <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a>. Last updated: {upd}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
